From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:55:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: let a panel turn off command-mode MDP burst

DSI 6G v1.3+ always sets CMD_MODE_MDP_CTRL2.BURST_MODE. The Surface Duo's LG panels show a garbled or black picture
with it (Microsoft's kernel and UEFI leave it off). Add MIPI_DSI_MODE_NO_CMD_BURST: when the panel sets it the host
clears BURST_MODE.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c | 5 ++++-
 include/drm/drm_mipi_dsi.h         | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
index 3945aafcc..c140c922d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -823,8 +823,11 @@ static void dsi_ctrl_enable(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host,
 		if (cfg_hnd->major == MSM_DSI_VER_MAJOR_6G) {
 			data = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_CMD_MODE_MDP_CTRL2);
 
-			if (cfg_hnd->minor >= MSM_DSI_6G_VER_MINOR_V1_3)
+			if (cfg_hnd->minor >= MSM_DSI_6G_VER_MINOR_V1_3 &&
+			    !(msm_host->mode_flags & MIPI_DSI_MODE_NO_CMD_BURST))
 				data |= DSI_CMD_MODE_MDP_CTRL2_BURST_MODE;
+			else
+				data &= ~DSI_CMD_MODE_MDP_CTRL2_BURST_MODE;
 
 			if (msm_dsi_host_is_wide_bus_enabled(&msm_host->base))
 				data |= DSI_CMD_MODE_MDP_CTRL2_DATABUS_WIDEN;
diff --git a/include/drm/drm_mipi_dsi.h b/include/drm/drm_mipi_dsi.h
index 0ddf1f52c..bfec040a8 100644
--- a/include/drm/drm_mipi_dsi.h
+++ b/include/drm/drm_mipi_dsi.h
@@ -140,6 +140,8 @@ struct mipi_dsi_host *of_find_mipi_dsi_host_by_node(struct device_node *node);
 #define MIPI_DSI_HS_PKT_END_ALIGNED	BIT(12)
 /* pack all DSC slices for a line into a single packet (backport of upstream) */
 #define MIPI_DSI_MODE_DSC_ALL_SLICES_IN_PKT	BIT(13)
+/* command mode: the panel needs the host's MDP burst mode off (one burst per line) */
+#define MIPI_DSI_MODE_NO_CMD_BURST	BIT(14)
 
 enum mipi_dsi_pixel_format {
 	MIPI_DSI_FMT_RGB888,
